  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Gravity Timer**\n\nI\'m focusing on the core concept: a \"Gravity Timer\" as a PWA, though initially within AI Studio. I\'m prioritizing React, responsiveness, and handling device motion. I\'m considering a functional simulation, which will need its own set of events.\n\n\n**Evaluating Feature Suitability**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the suitability of available skills for the \"Gravity Timer\" concept. Firebase integration appears unnecessary, considering local storage options for the timer\'s functionality. My focus is now shifting to ensure it supports gravity sensing in four phone orientations. I\'m prioritizing the responsive layout for consistent visual experience.\n\n\n**Refining Scope and Intent**\n\nI\'ve clarified the scope and aligned it strictly with the user\'s intent. My thoughts now prioritize a client-side solution using `localStorage` for data persistence. I\'m carefully avoiding any unnecessary features, particularly AI, to remain true to the user\'s explicit instructions. This means avoiding cloud components.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Sensor Implementation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the critical aspect: sensor implementation. I\'m prioritizing direct device orientation and motion event sensing for mobile. Crucially, I\'m developing a robust 3D/2D simulator for desktop users, ensuring complete feature parity and usability within AI Studio previews. I\'m focusing on user permission for device motion, particularly on iOS, through a dedicated button. The goal is gorgeous and functional, and to avoid unrequested features!\n\n\n**Planning the Aesthetic & Logic**\n\nMy focus is now on the visual design, considering custom fonts and beautiful sounds via the Web Audio API for timer cues, avoiding unreliable external assets. I\'m also planning local storage for timer history and stats. Importantly, the design will allow custom timer durations for each of the four directions, and a full-featured simulation panel! I\'m planning an interactive gravity simulator and real sensor integration, with a permission request workflow for iOS.\n\n\n**Defining Timer Behaviors**\n\nI\'m now detailing each orientation\'s timer state. Each direction will have a configurable label and duration, including a pomodoro-style setup. I\'m assigning face-up as pause and face-down as start/resume. I must ensure the user can customize each direction\'s timer details. Next, I\'m defining a custom PWA manifest.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will inspect the existing `metadata.json` to configure the application\'s name and description correctly."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 817816542
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
