  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Physical System**\n\nI\'ve decided to build the interactive physical particle system within a new `GravityParticlesCanvas.tsx` component, located in `/src/components/`, which will be imported into the `GravityTimer` component. This restructuring feels cleaner and makes more sense as a contained entity.\n\n\n**Defining Physics Parameters**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the physics implementation within the canvas. I\'ve settled on a fixed coordinate system for internal calculations (like `cx = 150`, `cy = 150`, `R = 120`), handling scaling through CSS. This simplifies physics and maintains consistency across devices. I\'m aiming for smooth particle movement: bouncing off walls and colliding with each other within the circular timer.\n\n\n**Enhancing Canvas Interaction**\n\nI\'m now integrating user interaction into the particle canvas. My goal is to allow users to add forces by clicking/dragging within the canvas area. This could simulate \"wind gusts\" or attraction/repulsion between particles. The design carefully avoids interfering with other buttons. I\'ve confirmed the central display has no interactive elements, making an interactive canvas safe.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 769682698
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
